'''Opeepit''' was a [[Frigosian]] [[Gender|male]] who lived on the ''[[Colossus]]'' refueling station during the [[New Republic Era|era]] of the [[New Republic]]. He was the station's sole janitor.

==Biography==
===Calm before the storm===
Opeepit was the janitor of the ''[[Colossus]]'' platform. When [[Kazuda Xiono]] first visited the [[Office of Acquisitions]], he went past the [[Frigosian]] while he cleaned the floor.<ref name="Recruit">{{Resistance|The Recruit}}</ref> When Xiono was running to stop [[Jace Rucklin]] from racing, he was blocked by Opeepit and a number of droids that were working in the corridor.<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" /> Later, Opeepit was carrying a trash bin around the [[Colossus marketplace|''Colossus'' marketplace]] while [[Tamara Ryvora]] and [[Synara San]] conversed nearby. After eating their [[Meiloorun fruit|meilooruns]], they put the rinds in the bin, which Opeepit then inspected. At one point, Opeepit was in the marketplace discarding contents of a trash bin into a dumpster while [[Neeku Vozo]] and [[Jarek Yeager]] were nearby, purchasing a [[gorg]] from [[Bolza Grool's gorg stand]].<ref name="Neeku's Reward">{{Resistance|Neeku's Reward}}</ref> Also in the marketplace, during a race between the members of [[Ace Squadron]], Opeepit was sweeping behind the watchful fans.<ref name="The Need for Speed">{{Resistance|The Need for Speed}}</ref> Later, [[pirate]]s [[Raid on the Colossus|attacked]] the ''Colossus''. Opeepit chased a [[Hassk]] pirate around with his [[floor sweeper]].<ref name="Synara's Score">{{Resistance|Synara's Score}}</ref> When Xiono, under order of [[Poe Dameron]], was investigating a potential link between [[Captain]] [[Imanuel Doza|Doza]] and the [[First Order]], he passed Opeepit, who was sweeping the hallway.<ref name="Secrets and Holograms">{{Resistance|Secrets and Holograms}}</ref>. Another time, [[Tamara Ryvora]] passed Opeepit, who was cleaning the docking pad, when she was searching for Neeku. Neeku had taken in what he thought was a stray baby [[Rokkna| rokkna]], whom he named [[Bibo]], but the ''Colossus'' soon came under attack by [[Bibo's mother]] who, unlike her child, was enormous. Opeepit was cleaning the marketplace when the attack began, prompting him to flee inside with everyone else.<ref name="Bibo">{{Resistance|Bibo (episode)}}</ref>

===Sweeper stolen===
[[File:OpeepitSonicMop-TheRecruitPart2.jpg|thumb|250px|Opeepit cleaning the floor]]
Following the First Order's [[Torra Doza's abduction|rescue]] of Torra from the [[Warbird gang]], First Order [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtroopers]] [[Occupation of the Colossus|occupied]] the ''Colossus''. Opeepit was talking to the [[Gotal]] [[Rolt]] in the marketplace when three stormtroopers harassed the [[Rodian]] [[Glem]]. He was later cleaning the hallway floors when two stormtroopers approached him and asked how long he had worked on the ''Colossus''. Opeepit, struggling to remember, replied in his [[Frigosian language| native language]], but the stormtroopers said they needed to take the sweeper. Opeepit resisted and attempted to pull it back, but one of the stormtroopers used their larger stature to intimidate him into stepping away. They walked off and Opeepit yelled at them, shaking his mechanical [[utility arm]] in protest, but he quickly lowered his head with a vocal dismay. Later that day, Xiono and San almost ran into him while exiting a [[turbolift]], which he responded to in verbal agitation. The two quickly apologized, and Opeepit made it clear he was just in a bad mood. Upon Xiono asking what was wrong, he complained about the confiscation. Xiono and San expressed their sympathy, but Opeepit just muttered to himself as he left the lift.<ref name="First Order Occupation" />

Without his floor sweeper, Opeepit was forced to clean the floors with a brush. While scrubbing at a hall intersection, a stormtrooper, who was actually the [[Resistance]] [[spy]] Kazuda Xiono in disguise, walked into the puddle and he told him to go around. As the trooper left, he annoyingly stated that Opeepit would clean the floors faster with a floor sweeper, which left him muttering sarcastically to himself. That evening, he was carrying a basket of [[fruit]] when the same stormtrooper pushed past him, knocking the fruit out of his hands. Enraged, Opeepit kicked one of the fruit aside as two stormtroopers passed him.<ref name="New Trooper">{{Resistance|The New Trooper}}</ref> Later, Opeepit was scrubbing the floors in the marketplace when the ''Colossus'' began sinking. Large doors sealed off the outside to prevent internal flooding, but not before some of the sea water poured into where Opeepit was cleaning.<ref name="Descent">{{Resistance|Descent (episode)}}</ref>

==Personality and traits==
Opeepit was a male Frigosian with [[Color|yellow]] hair and cybernetic hands.<ref name="Recruit" />

==Equipment==
Opeepit wore a breathing mask and heavy black goggles to protect him from [[Castilon]]'s atmosphere and light.<ref name="Recruit" /><ref name="Face of Evil">"[[The Face of Evil]]"</ref> He used a floor sweeper.<ref name="First Order Occupation" />

==Behind the scenes==
Opeepit was a character developed for the ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'' animated series. He first appeared in the [[Star Wars Resistance Season One|Season One]] premiere, "[[The Recruit]],"<ref name="Recruit" /> but was not identified until after his appearance in "[[Fuel for the Fire]],"<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" /> in ''[[Bucket's List]]''.<ref name="Bucket's List" /> He was voiced by [[Justin Ridge]].<ref name="Voice">{{Instagram|username=justinridgeart|url=p/C8NEVRsvMfk|name=[[Justin Ridge]]|date=2024-06-14|quote=Yep! I voiced Bucket and also the little janitor on the Colossus!|archivefile=File:JustinVoicesBucketAndOpeepit-Instagram.png}} {{C|In response to: Hi, I was wondering if you voiced a character on Star Wars resistance? If so, who did you voice?}}</ref>

